E3	openrouter	\N	v1.0	GENERAL	{"answer": "The boundary for Scope 2 emissions applies to the consumption of purchased or acquired electricity, heating, cooling, or steam, as applicable.", "run_id": "SEBI-BRSR-2023", "grounded": true, "citations": [{"doc": "SEBI BRSR Guidance Note", "text": "Disclose Scope 2 greenhouse gas emissions arising from the consumption of purchased or acquired electricity, heating, cooling or steam, as applicable.", "score": null, "section": "Principle 6 - Essential Indicator 3", "version": "BRSR-2023"}], "is_fallback": false, "indicator_code": "GENERAL"}	1.0000	\N	5398	proposed	\N	\N	\N	7730c51a-1e4c-4b13-bc38-fe7830becd59	2026-10-10 04:55:18.907776+05:30	2026-10-10 04:55:18.907794+05:30
E3	openrouter	\N	v1.0	GENERAL	{"answer": "Renewable Energy Certificates (RECs) are accounted for in the SEBI BRSR framework to promote the development and use of renewable energy sources.", "run_id": "ESG-2023-001", "grounded": true, "citations": [{"doc": "BRSR Guidance Note", "text": "RECs are a tradable commodity that represents the environmental attributes of one megawatt-hour (MWh) of electricity generated from an eligible renewable energy source.", "score": 8.5, "section": "BRSR Guidance Note", "version": "BRSR-2023"}, {"doc": "BRSR Guidance Note", "text": "The organization discloses the total amount of RECs purchased or sold during the reporting period.", "score": null, "section": "GRI 303: Energy", "version": "GRI 2020"}, {"doc": "BRSR Guidance Note", "text": "RECs are used to verify the origin of renewable energy and ensure that the energy is actually generated from renewable sources.", "score": 9.0, "section": "GHG Protocol", "version": "GHGP 2018"}], "is_fallback": false, "indicator_code": "ESG-REC-001"}	1.0000	\N	2417	proposed	\N	\N	\N	a9599a64-a522-42ea-b587-821b33bc6b9f	2026-10-10 05:12:00.509988+05:30	2026-10-10 05:12:00.51001+05:30
E3	openrouter	\N	v1.0	GENERAL	{"answer": "Scope 1, Scope 2, and Scope 3 emissions refer to the different categories of greenhouse gas (GHG) emissions that a company is required to disclose under the SEBI BRSR guidelines.", "run_id": "SEBI-BRSR-2023", "grounded": true, "citations": [{"doc": "BRSR Guidance Note", "text": "Disclose Scope 1 greenhouse gas emissions arising from sources owned or controlled by the company, including stationary combustion and mobile combustion where applicable.", "score": null, "section": "Principle 6 - Essential Indicator 3", "version": "BRSR-2023"}], "is_fallback": false, "indicator_code": "GHG-SCOPE"}	1.0000	\N	4937	proposed	\N	\N	\N	9de7fb03-6cb1-48bf-a93f-2f3009597553	2026-10-10 05:12:22.132928+05:30	2026-10-10 05:12:22.132953+05:30
E3	openrouter	\N	v1.0	GENERAL	{"answer": "A BRSR report is a comprehensive document that outlines a company's business responsibility and sustainability performance.", "run_id": "SEBI-BRSR-2023", "grounded": true, "citations": [{"doc": "SEBI LODR Regulation 34(2)(f)", "text": "The report must provide a clear and transparent picture of the company's ESG performance and risks.", "score": null, "section": "Business Responsibility and Sustainability Reporting", "version": "BRSR-2023"}, {"doc": "GRI Standards", "text": "The report must be prepared in accordance with the GRI Standards and provide a comprehensive overview of the company's sustainability performance.", "score": null, "section": "Sustainability Reporting", "version": "GRI 2020"}], "is_fallback": false, "indicator_code": "GENERAL"}	1.0000	\N	6904	proposed	\N	\N	\N	40d19fb7-fb18-417f-ac05-ee6755ba9241	2026-10-10 05:12:48.185262+05:30	2026-10-10 05:12:48.185281+05:30
E3	openrouter	\N	v1.0	GENERAL	{"answer": "A BRSR report is a comprehensive disclosure document that provides stakeholders with insights into a company's business responsibility and sustainability performance.", "run_id": "SEBI-BRSR-2023-001", "grounded": true, "citations": [{"doc": "BRSR Guidance Note", "text": "The Securities and Exchange Board of India (Listing Obligations and Disclosure Requirements) Regulations, 2015", "score": null, "section": "Regulation 34(2)(f) of SEBI LODR", "version": "BRSR-2023"}, {"doc": "BRSR Guidance Note", "text": "Business Responsibility and Sustainability Reporting (BRSR) Guidance Note, 2023", "score": null, "section": "BRSR Guidance Note", "version": "BRSR-2023"}], "is_fallback": false, "indicator_code": "GENERAL"}	1.0000	\N	1817	proposed	\N	\N	\N	bcf208a9-4504-4471-966a-dc4598245e77	2026-10-10 05:13:09.177546+05:30	2026-10-10 05:13:09.177568+05:30
