E3	openrouter	\N	v1.0	GENERAL	{"answer": "• **Regulatory Purpose**: Renewable energy certificates (RECs) are accounted for to promote the development and use of renewable energy sources, as per Regulation 34(2)(f) of SEBI LODR. This encourages companies to invest in renewable energy projects and reduce their carbon footprint.\\n• **Scope & Boundary**: The scope of RECs includes all types of renewable energy sources, such as solar, wind, and hydroelectric power. The boundary of RECs is defined by the SEBI BRSR framework, which requires companies to report on their renewable energy consumption and generation.\\n• **Calculation Rules**: Companies calculate RECs based on the amount of renewable energy generated or consumed, as per the GRI Standards and GHG Protocol. The calculation rules are outlined in the BRSR Core, which provides a framework for reporting on ESG metrics.\\n• **Disclosure Requirements**: Companies are required to disclose their REC data in their BRSR reports, which are publicly available on the SEBI website. This transparency promotes accountability and enables stakeholders to make informed decisions.\\n• **Audit Verification**: The audit process involves verifying the accuracy of REC data, including the calculation of RECs and disclosure of REC data in the BRSR report.", "run_id": "ESG-1234", "grounded": true, "citations": [{"doc": "BRSR Guidance Note", "text": "Renewable Energy Certificates", "score": null, "section": "Section 3.2", "version": "BRSR-2023"}], "is_fallback": false, "indicator_code": "ESG-001"}	1.0000	\N	2568	proposed	\N	\N	\N	6f628047-d0f4-4581-a150-9b076cd9c9ef	2026-10-11 11:38:26.225927+05:30	2026-10-11 11:38:26.225942+05:30
