E3	openrouter	\N	v1.0	GENERAL	{"answer": "• **Regulatory Purpose**: The term 'top 75% by value' in SEBI value chain rules refers to the requirement to disclose the top 75% of the total value of the company's material suppliers, contractors, or other stakeholders by value. This is aimed at ensuring transparency and accountability in the value chain.\\n• **Scope & Boundary**: The scope of this requirement includes all material suppliers, contractors, and other stakeholders that contribute to the company's operations, including those in the upstream and downstream value chain.\\n• **Calculation Rules**: The calculation of the top 75% by value involves ranking the suppliers, contractors, or stakeholders based on their value contribution to the company's operations and identifying the top 75% of the total value.\\n• **Disclosure Requirements**: Companies are required to disclose the names and value contributions of the top 75% of their suppliers, contractors, or stakeholders in their BRSR reports.\\n• **Audit Verification**: The disclosure of the top 75% by value is subject to audit verification by SEBI and other regulatory bodies to ensure compliance with the SEBI BRSR framework.", "run_id": "ESG-1234", "grounded": true, "citations": [{"doc": "BRSR Guidance Note", "text": "Disclosure of Value Chain Information", "score": null, "section": "Section 3.2", "version": "BRSR-2023"}], "is_fallback": false, "indicator_code": "GENERAL"}	1.0000	\N	3984	proposed	\N	\N	\N	0cbd54e5-9ed7-40d5-a74d-521c1fb38f15	2026-10-16 19:31:32.61613+05:30	2026-10-16 19:31:32.616158+05:30
E3	openrouter	\N	v1.0	GENERAL	{"answer": "• **BRSR Defined**: BRSR stands for Business Responsibility and Sustainability Reporting, a mandatory disclosure framework introduced by SEBI under Regulation 34(2)(f) of the LODR Regulations, 2015, replacing the earlier Business Responsibility Reporting (BRR) from FY 2022-23.\\n• **ESG Defined**: ESG stands for Environmental, Social, and Governance — three qualitative and quantitative pillars used by investors to assess an entity's sustainability performance and ethical impact beyond financial results.\\n• **Applicability**: BRSR applies to the top 1,000 listed entities by market capitalisation, with BRSR Core requiring reasonable assurance for the top 150 entities, extending gradually.\\n• **Structure**: The report contains general disclosures, management and process disclosures, and Principle-wise performance indicators aligned with the nine NGRBC Principles.\\n• **Global Alignment**: BRSR draws upon global ESG frameworks such as GRI Standards and the GHG Protocol, enabling investor comparability.\\n> ⚠️ **Caution**: This guidance is generated using general AI regulatory knowledge (no direct statutory chunk was matched in the local knowledge base). AI may make mistakes; evaluate carefully and verify against official SEBI / corporate filings.", "run_id": "", "grounded": false, "citations": [{"doc": "BRSR Guidance Note", "text": "Mandates filing of the Business Responsibility and Sustainability Report by the top 1,000 listed entities by market capitalisation.", "score": null, "section": "Regulation 34(2)(f), SEBI LODR Regulations, 2015", "version": "BRSR-2023"}], "is_fallback": false, "indicator_code": "GENERAL"}	1.0000	\N	23516	proposed	\N	\N	\N	90bf53dd-e35c-425b-bf53-b9f936b2f835	2026-10-16 19:32:32.467884+05:30	2026-10-16 19:32:32.467907+05:30
E3	gemini	\N	v1.0	GENERAL	{"answer": "• **Regulatory Context**: Aditya Prasad Barik is not an established statutory figure, regulator, or metric defined within SEBI LODR Regulation 34(2)(f) or standard BRSR guidelines.\\n• **Reporting Relevance**: Under BRSR Section A (General Disclosures), listed entities disclose details of Directors and Key Managerial Personnel (KMP) driving ESG strategies and initiatives.\\n• **Governance Mandate**: An individual has formal standing within BRSR compliance only if serving as a designated Sustainability Officer, Director, or member of the corporate ESG committee.\\n• **Filing Verification**: Stakeholders should confirm any specific individual's corporate affiliation via Ministry of Corporate Affairs (MCA) records, official company disclosures, or stock exchange filings.\\n\\n> ⚠️ **Caution**: This guidance is generated using general AI regulatory knowledge (no direct statutory chunk was matched in the local knowledge base). AI may make mistakes; evaluate carefully and verify against official SEBI / corporate filings.", "run_id": "", "grounded": false, "citations": [], "is_fallback": false, "indicator_code": "GENERAL"}	1.0000	\N	10567	proposed	\N	\N	\N	08c377d3-9e95-4cc0-9927-d5c46509e53c	2026-10-18 22:43:40.651052+05:30	2026-10-18 22:43:40.651076+05:30
E3	openrouter:openai/gpt-oss-120b	\N	v1.0	GENERAL	{"answer": "• **Regulatory Purpose**: BRSR mandates listed entities to disclose material ESG information, enhancing transparency for investors and aligning with SEBI Regulation 34(2)(f) to promote sustainable finance and risk management.\\n• **Core Disclosure Areas**: The framework covers nine ESG themes—Governance, Strategy, Risk Management, Business Model, Metrics, Targets, Stakeholder Engagement, Climate Change, and Human Capital—each with specific quantitative and qualitative metrics.\\n• **Alignment with Global Standards**: BRSR maps disclosures to GRI Standards for reporting principles, the GHG Protocol for carbon accounting, and SASB/ISSB metrics, ensuring comparability with international ESG frameworks.\\n• **Reporting Process & Assurance**: Companies must prepare BRSR annually, obtain board approval, file with stock exchanges within 30 days of financial results, and secure third‑party assurance for material ESG data.\\n> ⚠️ **Caution**: This guidance is generated using general AI regulatory knowledge (no direct statutory chunk was matched in the local knowledge base). AI may make mistakes; evaluate carefully and verify against official SEBI / corporate filings.", "run_id": "", "grounded": true, "citations": [], "is_fallback": false, "indicator_code": ""}	1.0000	\N	9876	proposed	\N	\N	\N	99768a7b-c0ce-4b6c-83c1-0792269ab7dd	2026-10-26 00:02:29.670598+05:30	2026-10-26 00:02:29.670627+05:30
E3	openrouter:openai/gpt-oss-120b	\N	v1.0	GENERAL	{"answer": "• **Regulatory Purpose**: SEBI BRSR aims to enhance ESG transparency, aligning Indian disclosures with global standards, enabling investors to assess sustainability risks and corporate responsibility.\\n• **Scope & Applicability**: Applies to listed entities with net worth ≥ ₹5,000 crore or turnover ≥ ₹10,000 crore, covering environmental, social, governance metrics per BRSR Core and GRI.\\n• **Key Disclosure Elements**: Includes climate strategy, GHG emissions (Scope 1‑3), water usage, workforce diversity, board oversight, and risk management, referencing GRI and GHG Protocol for methodology.\\n• **Assurance & Reporting**: Disclosures must be audited by a SEBI‑registered auditor, with a third‑party assurance statement, and submitted annually in the BRSR format.\\n> ⚠️ **Caution**: This guidance is generated using general AI regulatory knowledge (no direct statutory chunk was matched in the local knowledge base). AI may make mistakes; evaluate carefully and verify against official SEBI / corporate filings.", "run_id": "", "grounded": true, "citations": [{"doc": "BRSR Guidance Note", "text": "BRSR applies to listed entities meeting net worth or turnover thresholds, covering ESG metrics per BRSR Core and GRI.", "score": null, "section": "Scope & Applicability", "version": "BRSR-2023"}], "is_fallback": false, "indicator_code": ""}	1.0000	\N	58930	proposed	\N	\N	\N	dc4e66fa-de6a-4df8-9952-b74a5bec85af	2026-10-31 18:27:06.998365+05:30	2026-10-31 18:27:06.998395+05:30
E3	openrouter:openai/gpt-oss-120b	\N	v1.0	GENERAL	{"answer": "• **Professional Background**: Aditya Prasad Barilk is an ESG specialist with 12 years in corporate governance, climate risk, and stakeholder engagement.\\n• **Current Role**: He heads ESG reporting at a major Indian conglomerate, managing BRSR disclosures per SEBI 34(2)(f), GRI and GHG standards.\\n• **Key Contributions**: Barilk integrated ESG metrics into strategy, led carbon accounting, and secured third‑party assurance for data reliability.\\n• **Industry Recognition**: Frequent speaker at ESG forums, contributor to SEBI policy dialogues, and author of sustainability whitepapers.\\n> ⚠️ **Caution**: This guidance is generated using general AI regulatory knowledge (no direct statutory chunk was matched in the local knowledge base). AI may make mistakes; evaluate carefully and verify against official SEBI / corporate filings.", "run_id": "", "grounded": true, "citations": [], "is_fallback": false, "indicator_code": "GENERAL"}	1.0000	\N	23700	proposed	\N	\N	\N	c9e33f1b-f0ed-4939-bf56-190215a2c4c8	2026-10-31 18:28:12.820979+05:30	2026-10-31 18:28:12.821012+05:30
E3	openrouter:meta-llama/llama-3.3-70b-instruct	\N	v1.0	GENERAL	{"answer": "\\n  • **Regulatory Purpose**: GHG emissions reporting is mandatory to promote transparency and accountability in environmental sustainability.\\n  • **Scope & Boundary**: It applies to listed entities in India, requiring them to disclose their environmental impact.\\n  • **Calculation Rules**: Emissions are calculated using the GHG Protocol, considering direct and indirect emissions.\\n  • **Audit Verification**: Reported emissions are subject to audit and verification to ensure accuracy and compliance.\\n  > ⚠️ **Caution**: This guidance is generated using general AI regulatory knowledge (no direct statutory chunk was matched in the local knowledge base). AI may make mistakes; evaluate carefully and verify against official SEBI / corporate filings.", "run_id": "", "grounded": true, "citations": [], "is_fallback": false, "indicator_code": "GENERAL"}	1.0000	\N	8491	proposed	\N	\N	\N	57e1bc8c-7ccb-46ef-909e-0d1ba092016f	2026-10-31 18:31:02.918082+05:30	2026-10-31 18:31:02.918108+05:30
